  "name": "copernicus-glofas-initial-conditions",
  "notes": "The Global Flood Awareness System (GloFAS) initial conditions describe the\nhydrometeorological state of the land surface that drives the hydrological forecast\nmodel. This dataset contains daily raster GeoTIFFs for precipitation accumulation,\nsnow melt, snow cover, and soil moisture.\n\nAnomaly layers show deviation from climatological norms and help identify conditions\nthat may precondition basins for flooding or drought.",
